// Twists: what the phone can do to the live state (DEVIATIONS.md 4). The board
// applies one between ticks after checking only that it is well formed: it
// parses, the kind is known, every id is a registry row or a gene in the
// genome. There are no caps, with one rule: basic food is body-only (ask 15),
// so the phone never drops a pellet or fires a meal. It brings special treats
// instead, each a row here whose effect no pellet has. A row plus
// twist_<name> in src/twists.cpp is the whole change; SCHEMA streams the args
// so the website needs no release. Ids may be given by registry name or by number.
//
// BLORB_TWIST(name, args)
BLORB_TWIST(stimulus,  "<stim>")                                  // fired as if sensed, at the next tick; not button or fed
BLORB_TWIST(gene_edit, "<uid> <offset> <value>")                  // one body byte; checkpointed in the lineage
BLORB_TWIST(rename,    "<name>")                                  // 1..15 of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -
BLORB_TWIST(pick,      "<egg>")                                   // choose a clutch egg
BLORB_TWIST(prophecy,  "<feature> <action> <drive> <permille>")   // set one brain weight
BLORB_TWIST(prophecy_treat, "")                                   // a treat baked from the phone's futures: vision, so he glows; no food
